            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis of intracardiac thrombus by 99mTc-MAA scintiscanning.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>175-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Because of its capacity to form a deposit on thrombus fibrin, 99mTc-macroaggregated albumin can be used to detect intracardiac thrombus by routine imaging. The authors report a case of right ventricular thrombus diagnosed antemortem on a routine lung study in a patient with an intracardiac hyperalimentation catheter in place.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
